  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Two complete LRO families, stacked",
      "items": [
        "cbct-anatomy-segmentation and -computation are each a front plus a worker",
        "Both fronts are the same twenty-line lro.SetupHandler setup, so nothing is bespoke",
        "Both also call SetExtractExternalRefs, which the plain dia families do not"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Where the orchestration lives",
      "items": [
        "The tier 1 worker has no client/ or proto/ directory and no compute container",
        "It resolves tooth-recognition first, then cbct-anatomy-segmentation-computation",
        "parl-worker is the only other MLE worker with this exact shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Version mapping is a hard gate",
      "items": [
        "A per-downstream version map is read for the requested semantic version",
        "A miss raises no version mapping found for the service, it does not fall back",
        "Both downstream names are constants at worker.go lines 22 and 23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "The heaviest pod MLE runs",
      "items": [
        "The tier 2 sidecar requests 3 CPU and 20Gi and may burst to 5 CPU and 30Gi",
        "That is the largest memory ceiling of any MLE compute container",
        "LRO threshold is 17 minutes under DIA-019, matched only by cbct-segmentation"
      ]
    }
  ]
